  "claim": "Six amended native Claude coding attempts passed shared visible, held-out and scope checks. All three selective-policy attempts chose native computation; observed aggregate usage was 2.42% higher than the native policy, without a Context Mode treatment. One earlier rejected integration attempt remains in campaign task totals.",
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic local integration pilot on one accepted coding fixture; not an upstream benchmark, whole-stack savings rate or universal model comparison.",
    "Three AB/BA/AB pairs partly counterbalance order; native cache warmth is uncontrolled and models have no fixed seed. No Context Mode calls occurred, so the tool's causal token or latency effect is unidentified.",
    "Hooks are disabled equally per invocation and a strict Context Mode-only MCP configuration is used. This controlled pilot is not normal-hook full-stack E2E.",
    "Usage means final native-reported cumulative modelUsage counted once per fresh task. Ordinary input, cache creation, cache reads and output are disjoint here; thinking is included in output.",
    "Coordinator, independent review, acceptance execution, reporting and any unreported provider requests are outside these task usage totals. Wall time covers the native subprocess only.",
    "Native list-price cost estimates are preserved in original usage fields; subscription billing and money saved are unknown.",
    "Private raw transcripts, session identifiers, commands and local paths are not published. Artifact hashes bind retained evidence but are not independent provider attestation.",
    "Initial protocol failed its workflow/scope contract despite passing product and final file-scope checks; that attempt is excluded only from amended quality-equivalent pairs and retained in all-attempt totals."
  ],
